# Files that run on the Linux server are checked out with LF on every platform, so a scp from a
# Windows working copy cannot carry a carriage return into bash, systemd, nginx or an rclone key
# (it did, three times on 2026-09-11). Enforced by tools/check_known_bugs.py (be-crlf-in-server-files).
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
